---
title: Why Astro Islands
publishDate: 2026-09-25
description: Shipping mostly-static HTML with a few interactive React components.
---

Most of this site needs no JavaScript at all — a sidebar toggle and a markdown
renderer are the only interactive pieces. Astro's **islands architecture** lets
each page ship as static HTML by default, with only the components marked
`client:load` hydrating in the browser.

## The trade-off

| Approach | JS shipped | Interactivity |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Full SPA | Everything | Everywhere |
| Traditional SSG | None | Nowhere |
| Astro islands | Only what's marked | Only where needed |

For a content site like this one, islands are close to the sweet spot: fast
first paint, small bundles, and the sidebar still toggles instantly.
